Z||000000||JetroGT||03-30-2001||11:07 PM||||I was going to enjoy the nice weather in the GT today. But when I went to start it, it had a lumpy idle. So I pop the trunk and take a look. The EGR valve is "floating" above the cross-over pipe. The thing had broken in half. The only thing holding it together was the plunger. I ordered a new EGR valve and a new selinoid from the dealer then went back home to remove the old parts. The valve came off easily. When I went to take the selinoid off I discovered that the hose running from the selinoid to the fire wall was not even connected! It had rotted off. It had always ran poorley, now I know why. And the funny thing is that the engine light never came on. Strange. <BR>||||reg||1
